 sauva / Property                                                                 Default Ignorable

 Current value · U+200D
   Yes
   Included in Default_Ignorable_Code_Point.

 Overview
   Identifies code points normally omitted from fallback display when their intended behavior is
   unsupported.

 Values
 > Yes — Included in Default_Ignorable_Code_Point.
   No — Not included; this does not guarantee a visible glyph.

 Notes
   These characters can affect surrounding text. This property is not a recommendation to delete
   them. Sauva may show a label to make them identifiable.

 Reference
   Unicode 17.0 · §5.21 Ignoring Characters in Processing
   https://www.unicode.org/versions/Unicode17.0.0/core-spec/chapter-5/#G40025








